																		A Really Weird Dream
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-sage-evergreen" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6043564); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6043564&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607678008" alt="Dr Sage Evergreen" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6043564)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-sage-evergreen" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6043564); return false;" >Dr Sage Evergreen</a></span> <span class="odate time_1591150645 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Jun 2020 02:17</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4674586">
									

<p>I think this post might be a bit on the longer end. So, if you're easily bored, I recommend picking something else to read.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I just woke up from a nap, and it's had to be the weirdest dream in my life. I fell asleep on top of my chemistry homework, and the last thing I remember crossing my mind before nodding off was Astral Projection. I don't know why I was thinking about it. All I remember was just imagining floating, and just sort of feeling like my limbs were flailing around, even though I knew my body wasn't moving. And then, the next thing I knew, I was awake (I was still dreaming, of course). I was still in the same spot I had fallen asleep in, except it was early daytime instead of late afternoon (the time that I'd fallen asleep). I knew because there were birds singing, and the sun outside was a lot brighter than when I fell asleep. Anyways, I opened my bedroom blinds to let in the light, and I just see this giant cat's face staring at me. It wasn't a normal cat though. It was more like if someone crossed cheshire cat, momo, and grumpy cat, then blew it up to about twenty times the initial size. And it was just staring at me through the window. Obviously, I flip out, I go to tell my parents, but they're busy arguing about something&#8230;I have no idea what, and they don't normally argue. But they kept shushing me when I tried telling them about the cat.</p>
<p>I tried going outside to my house into my backyard to see the cat, but I think it attacks me or looks at me or something. But then I'm suddenly tumbling down a hillside, and my head crashes into something, then I get knocked out. I wake up again, and I'm in the same exact place in my room. I re-open the window, same chesire cat, same freakout, same tumbling down a hill, and repeat for about five times. And the weirdest thing is, even though I know I'm 100% awake right now, I can still feel my forehead throbbing from smacking against&#8230;something. I don't know what. I was out gardening earlier today, so something might have hit me then. My head doesn't hurt or anything&#8230;it just fields weird.</p>
<p>But fifth time proves to be the charm, and when I go outside, the cat doesn't attack me. It just looks at me. I then see that it's on my neighbor's property instead of my own property. Somehow, I get my school counselor (don't ask me WHY he ended up in my dream) to come look at the cat, and he agrees that it's creepy and that it shouldn't be there. I don't see the cat for most of the dream, so that's a plus.</p>
<p>Then I go driving with my dad to go pick up flowers from a family friend's garden. (Okay, so note this is something that happened earlier today. I was trying to start a butterfly garden in my back yard, and we had a family friend that lives about 20 minutes away, so me and my dad actually drove to her house today to pick up the plants.) And that's when things start getting really weird. The sky somehow turns bloodred, like the sun is setting, except the sun is still high in the sky. And when we're driving, we drive past all these machines, which I'm pretty sure were grinders. We also drive through a city called which I think was called Greensboro. My dad tells me to remember Greensboro, because &quot;Greensboro is where everything happens&quot;. We finally arrive at the family friend's house, and she seems normal enough. But the plants are just really off. The flowers are all the wrong colors. And they just looked off. I'm not sure how to describe them. They just looked weird. But nonetheless, we took them.</p>
<p>And then I remember falling again. The same tumbling sensation I had with the chesire cat. And then I woke up again, except I was driving on the freeway. It was pitch-black, with the exception of my headlights lighting up the bumper of this white jeep in front of me. I could see the back of the head of the man n the front, and he seemed slumped over. I almost crash into him about 5 times, and I have a major panic attack every time I do. My dad isn't with me in the car. (I'm a minor, and I'm not allowed to drive by myself.) But every time I get too close to the car, he just appears in the backseat behind me and begins screeching at me. I think he even tried to choke me or hurt me in some way. (My dad is extremely kind and nice to me. He's never done anything like this to me, and the two of us have a really close and good relationship. I feel really bad for even dreaming he'd do something like that to me).</p>
<p>But as I was driving behind the white jeep, we eventually drive by Greensboro again. And I eventually get pissed at the car in front of me, and try to pass him at an intersection. Except, when I drive next to the man, his face is rotting. It's completely black, and you can see the flesh just starting to drip off of his skull. I think I could actually see the bone. At this point, I'm terrified, and my dad re-appears next to me and starts strangling me. Then I remember myself being thrown out of the car and hitting my head again. Then I actually woke up. I was in the same place I'd fallen asleep, and I could hear my mom calling me to get dinner.</p>
<p>It took me a while to make sure I was actually awake. But luckily, I am. Things make sense again. I'm pretty relieved, and I think I almost cried a couple of times. It's nighttime right now. I'm tempted to open up my bedroom blinds to make sure there's no cat staring back at me, but I'm too scared to do it. I think my dad noticed I wasn't talking to him as much as I normally do, and my entire family picked up on me acting weird. After I had dinner, I came straight to my laptop and started typing up the story. This is all I remember. If I made something up, or if I left something out, I'm really sorry. But this is everything I remember.</p>
<p>But that brings me to my final point: why type this out here, of all places?</p>
<p>I think I've been reading about/listening/writing/roleplaying/thinking about SCP a little bit too much. I have no idea if I'm overreacting or something, or if it just has to do with me being stressed and overwhelmed with school, or something else, but I just think it has something to do with me being on the SCP wiki. Has anyone here had a similar experience? Its been about two hours since I've woken up, and I haven't been able to get it off my mind. I want to be able to forget about this and dismiss it as a silly nightmare or some other crap like that, but I'm low key too terrified to even step out of my room right now. Well, with any hope, I'll be able to forget about this and move on soon. Who knows? Maybe I might even make an SCP out of this dream.</p>
</div>
